-- Representative example only. build_custom_property_query() in poller.py builds this text
-- at runtime, once per name in SWIS_GPS_CUSTOM_PROPERTIES plus SWIS_CITY_CUSTOM_PROPERTY.
-- Property names cannot be bound as SWQL parameters (parameters are values, not
-- identifiers), so each name is formatted into the query text, but only after it has been
-- confirmed against Orion.CustomProperty (see discover_custom_properties.swql) and passed
-- through _safe_identifier()'s allowlist regex. This file shows the shape for one property
-- named ExampleGpsField, which does not exist on any real server, so
-- SolarWinds_OrionGuides/tools/validate_swql.py correctly reports it as an unknown property.
-- That failure is expected: this demonstrates the pattern, not a literal query the poller
-- ships unmodified.
SELECT n.NodeID, n.CustomProperties.ExampleGpsField AS PropValue
FROM Orion.Nodes n
WHERE n.CustomProperties.ExampleGpsField IS NOT NULL
